<BaseLayout title="Privacy | Orchha Palace" description="How the Orchha Palace website handles booking, enquiry and analytics information." stickyBooking={false}>
  <article class="legal-page"><div class="legal-page__content shell"><p class="eyebrow">Website policy</p><h1>Privacy</h1><p>Last reviewed: 1 September 2026</p><p>This website collects only the information needed to answer event enquiries, operate essential site functions and, with permission, understand website usage.</p><h2>Bookings and payment</h2><p>Room availability, booking and payment continue in the hotel's official booking engine and PayU environment. This custom website does not receive or store payment-card information. The booking provider's privacy terms apply once you leave this site.</p><h2>Event enquiries</h2><p>The event form sends the information you provide—including name, contact details and event requirements—to the hotel's sales and reservations teams through the configured email provider. Do not include payment details or sensitive identity documents.</p><h2>Analytics and cookies</h2><p>Optional analytics load only after you choose “Allow analytics”. If you choose “Only essential”, no analytics tag is loaded. Your preference is stored locally in your browser.</p><h2>Spam protection</h2><p>The event form may use Cloudflare Turnstile to reduce automated abuse. Turnstile validates the interaction without receiving the form message itself.</p><h2>Your choices</h2><p>To ask what information the hotel holds about an enquiry, request a correction, or ask for deletion where applicable, email <a href="mailto:info@orchhapalace.com">info@orchhapalace.com</a>.</p></div></article>
</BaseLayout>
